ues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible since 4.7 dev 2\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev (dbff09512) - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Mobile) - integrated AMD Radeon(TM) Graphics (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 31.0.21923.11000) - AMD Ryzen 5 5500U with Radeon Graphics (12 threads) - 7.33 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nRecent device ID change for keyboards and mice ( https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116274 ) seems to break some projects that use `InputEvent.device` property directly, see https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116274#issuecomment-4148337780\nOne of the solutions might be to make a project setting for this change to keep compatibility with existing projects. This project setting most likely should be enabled by default for new projects and disabled by default for existing projects.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUse this piece of code in a script to see the device IDs:\n```gdscript\nfunc _input(event: InputEvent) -> void:\n\tif event is InputEventKey or event is InputEventMouseButton or event is InputEventMouseMotion:\n\t\tprint(event.device)\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n```gdscript\nfunc _input(event: InputEvent) -> void:\n\tif event is InputEventKey or event is InputEventMouseButton or event is InputEventMouseMotion:\n\t\tprint(event.device)\n```","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","sta